cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural framework for describing how
  multidimensional real resource and capital states K and nominal or expectation
  structures P across multiple actors form a value field whose attraction is
  realized through the actors' actions and decisions A. Each actor's K represents
  resources, capital, and degrees of freedom that the actor can access and use,
  while each actor's P represents expectation structures that the actor can
  observe or reference and that can affect decision-making. K, P, and A are not
  assumed to be scalar variables or probability distributions. P is treated as
  a history-dependent expectation stock, while E[Delta K] is represented
  separately as an expectation flow for a specified interval rather than as a
  required intermediate variable in action generation. Actions can change both
  K and P. Non-agentic changes in K, such as depreciation or natural loss, are
  treated as a secondary exception rather than a separate core pathway. At
  aggregate scales, Delta P and Delta K can serve as principal proxies when full
  action tracking is too costly.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
